> My AC currently is -16, and that's with some rusty armour.  One last
> question for the moment; AC -16 seems brilliant to me, I don't think
> I've ever got below -1 or -2 before, but how good is it really? 

An AC of -16 is good enough to ascend.  But it depends on the type of
armor; you will need MR if you want to go deeper.  What you have to
fear, if you don't have MR, is that you step on a polymorph trap and
important pieces of your armor being destroyed.

If your rusted armor is just standard dwarven outfit then you should
not bother to rustproof that, replace it instead, there's enough lying
around in the mines.

Make that pieces of armor fireproof/rotproof/rustproof that you intend
to keep for a long time: speed boots, gauntlets of power, robe, etc.

Don't rely only on your AC.  Fight from distance.  Flee, if necessary.

